1. Write a description for a while loop.

    When we use a while loop, we will repeat our code.
    This type of loop will only repeat as long as a specified thing or condition stays true.
    When the condition that we stablished changes to false, then the while loop will end.

2. Write a description for a for loop.

    This other type of loop iterate a known number of times.
    We use this one to go through sequences like lists, numbers, or strings.

3. Compare a while loop to a for loop

    The for loop process every element in a list, the while loop promt a user until they enter the valid information.
